# DISCRIMINATING probe. The previous shape could not tell "the lookahead refused" from "the tick
# was left unconsumed", because both produce a reject. Here a catch-all CAN consume the tick, so:
#
#   H1  a gated rule still MATCHES inside `!` ⇒ !tick refuses  ⇒ strict REJECTS
#   H2  a gated rule matches nothing          ⇒ !tick vacuous  ⇒ catchall eats "'" ⇒ strict ACCEPTS
#
# loose REJECTS under both hypotheses, and is the sanity arm.
@profiles: ["strict", "loose"]

@entry: true
top := trivia lit_one !tick catchall trivia     -> {kind: "t"}

lit_one := trivia "1"                           -> {kind: "one"}
catchall := trivia /['a-z]/                     -> {kind: "c"}

@profiles: ["loose"]
tick := trivia "'"                              -> {kind: "tick"}

trivia := /[ \t\r\n]*/
